{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"dede3a8d0085f62e","name":"card_unit_a_36_apache","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/USA/Allegiance/units/card_unit_a_36_apache","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"A-36 APACHE","text":"When A-36 APACHE attacks, friendly ground units get +1+1.","flavorText":"The A-36 Apache was an American ground-attack and dive bomber aircraft used in WWII by the US Army Air Force and the Royal Air Force. The A-36 first came into service in 1943 and was used in in North Africa Campaign, and then later in the Allied invasion of Sicily and the China-Burma-Indian Theater. The aircraft looked very similar to the P-51A Mustang fighter but had two more .50 caliber machine guns inside the lower engine housing that shot through the propeller arc. The A-36 also had dive breaks installed which limited the dive speed to 630 km/h and made it a very accurate dive bomber. The A-36 Apache was used in service until 1945 but many were withdrawn from service in 1944 and replaced with the P-40 Warhawk and P-47 Thunderbolt. A total of 500 aircraft were manufactured.","faction":"USA","type":"fighter","rarity":"Uncommon","cost":6,"operationCost":2,"attack":4,"defense":4},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_a_36_apache","title":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_unit_a_36_apache_title","SourceString":"A-36 APACHE","LocalizedString":"A-36 APACHE"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::fighter","attack":4,"defense":4,"range":2,"faction":"EFactionEnum::USA","kredits":6,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_unit_a_36_apache_text","SourceString":"When A-36 APACHE attacks, friendly ground units get +1+1.","LocalizedString":"When A-36 APACHE attacks, friendly ground units get +1+1."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_unit_a_36_apache_history","SourceString":"The A-36 Apache was an American ground-attack and dive bomber aircraft used in WWII by the US Army Air Force and the Royal Air Force. The A-36 first came into service in 1943 and was used in in North Africa Campaign, and then later in the Allied invasion of Sicily and the China-Burma-Indian Theater. The aircraft looked very similar to the P-51A Mustang fighter but had two more .50 caliber machine guns inside the lower engine housing that shot through the propeller arc. The A-36 also had dive breaks installed which limited the dive speed to 630 km/h and made it a very accurate dive bomber. The A-36 Apache was used in service until 1945 but many were withdrawn from service in 1944 and replaced with the P-40 Warhawk and P-47 Thunderbolt. A total of 500 aircraft were manufactured.","LocalizedString":"The A-36 Apache was an American ground-attack and dive bomber aircraft used in WWII by the US Army Air Force and the Royal Air Force. The A-36 first came into service in 1943 and was used in in North Africa Campaign, and then later in the Allied invasion of Sicily and the China-Burma-Indian Theater. The aircraft looked very similar to the P-51A Mustang fighter but had two more .50 caliber machine guns inside the lower engine housing that shot through the propeller arc. The A-36 also had dive breaks installed which limited the dive speed to 630 km/h and made it a very accurate dive bomber. The A-36 Apache was used in service until 1945 but many were withdrawn from service in 1944 and replaced with the P-40 Warhawk and P-47 Thunderbolt. A total of 500 aircraft were manufactured."},"operationCost":2,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Uncommon","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::Expansion2019","returnSet":"ECardSetEnum::OceaniaStorm","EffectType":"ECardEffectTypes::Trigger","soundBlowUp":{"ObjectName":"SoundCue'AU_Exp_Aircraft_Medium_Cue'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Assets/Audio/Card_Blowups/AU_Exp_Aircraft_Medium_Cue.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/USA/t_apache.t_apache","SubPathString":""},"artist":"Roy Grinnell","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/A-36_APACHE.A-36_APACHE","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize"